            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia inquired about what remedies other countries provide for these rights."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 11,
              "start": 11
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, justice Souter questioned how domestic law should apply the treaty\u2019s substantive provisions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 31
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked whether the United States has a legal obligation to provide an effective remedy under the treaty."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter further questioned whether Virginia permits a collateral\u2011review claim of ineffective assistance based on Vienna Convention violations."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0003-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 73,
              "start": 73
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether the State has an obligation to inquire about the defendant\u2019s nationality and advise of consular rights."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0004-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 74,
              "start": 74
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts raised a question about the need to give Miranda warnings before asking about citizenship."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0004-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 75,
              "start": 75
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy followed up on whether the State must advise the defendant of consular rights during booking or interrogation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked whether any relief beyond suppression was being sought."
      }
