          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Peter Gartlan, counsel for petitioner (No. 04-10566), according to Peter Gartlan, counsel for petitioner (No. 04-10566), petitioner Moises Sanchez\u2011Llamas argues that Article\u202f36 of the Vienna Convention on Consular Relations gives individuals a right to be notified of their consular representation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The statements that the petitioner seeks to suppress occurred about eight hours after the initial arrest."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Stancil",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Stancil, petitioner claims that the State failed to provide the required consular notification, violating the Vienna Convention."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "State Department",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "c9044ca348d3091208da0ff7758e2cef72a2ec728c12e648db511515bb2d67de",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-c9044ca348d3-0004-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 75,
              "start": 75
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The State Department says it has taken extensive steps, such as training videos and consular\u2011notice cards, to ensure compliance with the treaty."
      }
    ],
